<title>PHILIPPINES: Foreign direct investment in Philippines rises.</title>
<headline>Foreign direct investment in Philippines rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign direct investment in the Philippines rose 6.8 percent in the first quarter of this year to $969 million, the country's Central Bank said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said the increase augured well for the continued development of the economy.</p>
<p>New direct investment, which accounted for 59 percent of the total, was up nine percent to $571 million.</p>
<p>Portfolio investment rose 4.2 percent to $398 million.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841 8914</p>
